IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`
IMPORT `sfaa-div1-interpretation`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Layer 1, Part 7 Division 1 Subdivision (2): the corporation's register of substantial shareholders (section 137C).
-- Periods of days ("within 14 days", "within 7 days") are counted by sfa-periods.l4 (P1: the day of the event is not counted); a copy sent on or before the last day is in time (fork register A3).

§ `s 137C: the corporation keeps a register of substantial shareholders`

-- src:28456 | 137C.—(1) A corporation must keep a register in which it must
-- src:28457 | immediately enter —
@ref s 137C(1) (keeping the register) (src:28456-28457)
GIVEN
    `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies (the answer to the question under section 130(2): a listed company, or a corporation with a primary listing)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137C(1) the corporation must keep a register` MEANS
    IF `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A corporation must keep a register"; the body is not a corporation as section 130(2) reads the word for Division 1

-- src:28456 | 137C.—(1) A corporation must keep a register in which it must
-- src:28457 | immediately enter —
-- src:28459 | (a) the names of persons from whom it has received a notice
-- src:28460 | under section 135; and
-- src:28462 | (b) against each name so entered, the information given in the
-- src:28463 | notice and, where it receives a notice under section 136 or
-- src:28464 | 137, the information given in that notice.
@ref s 137C(1) (entering the notice) (src:28456-28464)
GIVEN
    `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies (the answer to the question under section 130(2): a listed company, or a corporation with a primary listing)?
    `the corporation has received a notice under section 135, 136 or 137` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation received a notice under section 135, 136 or 137?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137C(1) the corporation must immediately enter the names and information in the register` MEANS
    IF `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` AND `the corporation has received a notice under section 135, 136 or 137`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the names of persons from whom it has received a notice under section 135" and the information in a notice under section 136 or 137

DECLARE `s 137C action` IS ONE OF
    `s 137C enter the names and information in the register`
    `s 137C send the copy of the register`

-- "immediately" is read as a window of nought days (fork register A6): an entry on the day the notice is received is in time, one a day later is not.
-- src:28456 | 137C.—(1) A corporation must keep a register in which it must
-- src:28457 | immediately enter —
-- src:28459 | (a) the names of persons from whom it has received a notice
-- src:28460 | under section 135; and
-- src:28462 | (b) against each name so entered, the information given in the
-- src:28463 | notice and, where it receives a notice under section 136 or
-- src:28464 | 137, the information given in that notice.
@ref s 137C(1) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:28456-28464)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 137C action`
`s 137C(1) the corporation must immediately enter the names and information in the register` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    MUST `s 137C enter the names and information in the register`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the names and information were not entered in the register immediately on receipt of the notice (section 137C(1))"

-- Subsection (2): where the register is kept. A register kept anywhere else is the text's no ("must keep").
-- src:28471 | (2) The corporation must keep the register at its registered office or,
-- src:28472 | if the corporation does not have a registered office, at its principal
-- src:28473 | place of business in Singapore and the register must be open for
-- src:28474 | inspection by a member of the corporation without charge, and by any
@ref s 137C(2) (the place) (src:28471-28474)
GIVEN
    `the corporation has a registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have a registered office?
    `the register is kept at the registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the register kept at the corporation's registered office?
    `the register is kept at the principal place of business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the register kept at the corporation's principal place of business in Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137C(2) the register is kept at the place the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the corporation has a registered office`
    THEN IF `the register is kept at the registered office`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The corporation must keep the register at its registered office"
    ELSE IF `the register is kept at the principal place of business in Singapore`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the corporation does not have a registered office, at its principal place of business in Singapore"

-- Inspection: free to a member; $2 "or such lesser sum as the corporation requires" for any other person, so $2 is the most that may be charged.
-- src:28471 | (2) The corporation must keep the register at its registered office or,
-- src:28472 | if the corporation does not have a registered office, at its principal
-- src:28473 | place of business in Singapore and the register must be open for
-- src:28474 | inspection by a member of the corporation without charge, and by any
-- src:28475 | other person on payment for each inspection of a sum of $2 or such
-- src:28476 | lesser sum as the corporation requires.
@ref s 137C(2) (inspection) (src:28471-28476)
GIVEN
    `the person inspecting the register is a member of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who wants to inspect the register a member of the corporation?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 137C(2) the most the corporation may charge for each inspection of the register, in Singapore dollars` MEANS
    IF `the person inspecting the register is a member of the corporation`
    THEN 0  -- "without charge"
    ELSE 2  -- "a sum of $2 or such lesser sum as the corporation requires"

-- Subsection (3): copies. $1 a page or less, paid in advance; the copy to be sent within 14 days after the request, or such longer period as the Authority allows in the particular case.
-- src:28480 | (3) A person may request the corporation to provide the person with
-- src:28481 | a copy of the register or any part of the register on payment in
-- src:28482 | advance of a sum of $1 or such lesser sum as the corporation requires
-- src:28483 | for every page or part thereof required to be copied, and the
@ref s 137C(3) (the charge) (src:28480-28483)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 137C(3) the most the corporation may charge in advance for each page copied, in Singapore dollars` MEANS
    1  -- "a sum of $1 or such lesser sum as the corporation requires for every page or part thereof"

-- src:28483 | for every page or part thereof required to be copied, and the
-- src:28484 | corporation must send the copy to that person within 14 days, or such
-- src:28485 | longer period as the Authority may allow in any particular case, after
-- src:28486 | the day on which the corporation received the request.
@ref s 137C(3) (the time) (src:28483-28486)
GIVEN
    `the day the corporation received the request for a copy` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the corporation receive the request for a copy of the register or part of it?
    `the Authority has allowed a longer period in the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority allowed a longer period for sending the copy in this particular case?
    `the last day of the longer period the Authority has allowed` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the longer period the Authority has allowed (leave any date if none)?
GIVETH A DATE
`s 137C(3) the last day for the corporation to send the copy` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has allowed a longer period in the particular case` AND (`the last day of the longer period the Authority has allowed` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the corporation received the request for a copy` 14 Days)
    THEN `the last day of the longer period the Authority has allowed`
    ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the corporation received the request for a copy` 14 Days

-- src:28483 | for every page or part thereof required to be copied, and the
-- src:28484 | corporation must send the copy to that person within 14 days, or such
-- src:28485 | longer period as the Authority may allow in any particular case, after
-- src:28486 | the day on which the corporation received the request.
@ref 2 s 137C(3) (in time) (src:28483-28486)
GIVEN
    `the day the corporation received the request for a copy` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the corporation receive the request for a copy of the register or part of it?
    `the Authority has allowed a longer period in the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority allowed a longer period for sending the copy in this particular case?
    `the last day of the longer period the Authority has allowed` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the longer period the Authority has allowed (leave any date if none)?
    `the day the corporation sent the copy` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the corporation send the copy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137C(3) the copy is sent in time` MEANS
    IF `the day the corporation sent the copy` AT MOST `s 137C(3) the last day for the corporation to send the copy` `the day the corporation received the request for a copy` `the Authority has allowed a longer period in the particular case` `the last day of the longer period the Authority has allowed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the corporation must send the copy to that person within 14 days, or such longer period as the Authority may allow in any particular case"; a period fixed in the text's own words (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (a))

-- The regulative rule counts days (the clock of a trace counts calendar days from the request).
-- src:28480 | (3) A person may request the corporation to provide the person with
-- src:28481 | a copy of the register or any part of the register on payment in
-- src:28482 | advance of a sum of $1 or such lesser sum as the corporation requires
-- src:28483 | for every page or part thereof required to be copied, and the
-- src:28484 | corporation must send the copy to that person within 14 days, or such
-- src:28485 | longer period as the Authority may allow in any particular case, after
-- src:28486 | the day on which the corporation received the request.
@ref s 137C(3) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:28480-28486)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 137C action`
`s 137C(3) the corporation must send the copy within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    MUST `s 137C send the copy of the register`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the copy was not sent within 14 days after the request was received (section 137C(3))"

-- Subsection (4): the Authority's written requirement; the corporation sends the copy within 7 days after receiving it.
-- src:28490 | (4) The Authority may at any time in writing require the
-- src:28491 | corporation to provide it with a copy of the register or any part of
-- src:28492 | the register and the corporation must send the copy to the Authority
-- src:28493 | within 7 days after the day on which the corporation received the
-- src:28494 | requirement.
@ref s 137C(4) (src:28490-28494)
GIVEN
    `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies (the answer to the question under section 130(2): a listed company, or a corporation with a primary listing)?
    `the Authority has required the corporation in writing to provide a copy of the register or part of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority required the corporation in writing to provide it with a copy of the register or part of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137C(4) the corporation must send the Authority a copy of the register` MEANS
    IF `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` AND `the Authority has required the corporation in writing to provide a copy of the register or part of it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Authority may at any time in writing require the corporation to provide it with a copy of the register or any part of the register and the corporation must send the copy"

-- src:28490 | (4) The Authority may at any time in writing require the
-- src:28491 | corporation to provide it with a copy of the register or any part of
-- src:28492 | the register and the corporation must send the copy to the Authority
-- src:28493 | within 7 days after the day on which the corporation received the
-- src:28494 | requirement.
@ref 2 s 137C(4) (the time) (src:28490-28494)
GIVEN
    `the day the corporation received the Authority's requirement` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the corporation receive the Authority's written requirement?
GIVETH A DATE
`s 137C(4) the last day for the corporation to send the copy to the Authority` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the corporation received the Authority's requirement` 7 Days

-- src:28490 | (4) The Authority may at any time in writing require the
-- src:28491 | corporation to provide it with a copy of the register or any part of
-- src:28492 | the register and the corporation must send the copy to the Authority
-- src:28493 | within 7 days after the day on which the corporation received the
-- src:28494 | requirement.
@ref 2 s 137C(4) (in time) (src:28490-28494)
GIVEN
    `the day the corporation received the Authority's requirement` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the corporation receive the Authority's written requirement?
    `the day the corporation sent the copy` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the corporation send the copy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137C(4) the copy is sent to the Authority in time` MEANS
    IF `the day the corporation sent the copy` AT MOST `s 137C(4) the last day for the corporation to send the copy to the Authority` `the day the corporation received the Authority's requirement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the corporation must send the copy to the Authority within 7 days after the day on which the corporation received the requirement"; a period fixed in the text's own words (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (a))

-- src:28490 | (4) The Authority may at any time in writing require the
-- src:28491 | corporation to provide it with a copy of the register or any part of
-- src:28492 | the register and the corporation must send the copy to the Authority
-- src:28493 | within 7 days after the day on which the corporation received the
-- src:28494 | requirement.
@ref s 137C(4) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:28490-28494)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 137C action`
`s 137C(4) the corporation must send the Authority the copy within 7 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    MUST `s 137C send the copy of the register`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the copy was not sent to the Authority within 7 days after the requirement was received (section 137C(4))"

-- src:28498 | (5) Any corporation which fails to comply with subsection (1), (2),
-- src:28499 | (3) or (4) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:28500 | to a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:28501 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of
-- src:28502 | a day during which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 137C(5) (src:28498-28502)
GIVEN
    `the corporation fails to comply with section 137C(1), (2), (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation fail to comply with section 137C(1), (2), (3) or (4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137C(5) the corporation is guilty of an offence of failing to comply with the register provisions` MEANS
    IF `the corporation fails to comply with section 137C(1), (2), (3) or (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("Any corporation which fails to comply with subsection (1), (2), (3) or (4)"), not that a corporation that complies is innocent

-- src:28498 | (5) Any corporation which fails to comply with subsection (1), (2),
-- src:28499 | (3) or (4) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:28500 | to a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:28501 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of
-- src:28502 | a day during which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref 2 s 137C(5) (the penalty) (src:28498-28502)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 137C(5) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- a fine not exceeding $50,000 and a further fine not exceeding $5,000 a day after conviction; no imprisonment is stated, so 0
    Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000

-- Subsection (6): a flat negative about what the corporation is "taken" to know; JUST TRUE states that it is not so taken, for a thing done under the Subdivision.
-- src:28506 | (6) A corporation is not, by reason of anything done under this
-- src:28507 | Subdivision —
-- src:28509 | (a) to be taken for any purpose of the Companies Act 1967 to
-- src:28510 | have notice of; or
-- src:28512 | (b) to be put upon inquiry as to,
-- src:28514 | a right of a person to or in relation to a share in the corporation.
@ref s 137C(6) (src:28506-28514)
GIVEN
    `the thing was done under Subdivision (2) of Division 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing done under Subdivision (2) of Division 1 of Part 7 (sections 135 to 137D)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137C(6) the corporation is not taken to have notice of, or to be put upon inquiry as to, a right in a share by reason of the thing done` MEANS
    IF `the thing was done under Subdivision (2) of Division 1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason of anything done under this Subdivision"; a thing done under another provision is outside it
